cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or cite this framework, please cite it as below."
title: "Freight Custody Verification Framework (FCVF)"
version: "0.1-draft"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
authors:
  - family-names: "Meng"
    given-names: "Lingyu"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add if you have one; free at orcid.org
type: "standard"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lym422/fcvf-spec"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23179115"
abstract: >
  An open framework specifying what a party that releases, receives, or carries truckload
  freight must do to verify, at each physical custody transfer, that the vehicle taking custody
  belongs to the carrier of record and that the load's seal is present and intact, and what
  record of that verification must be kept. Forty-eight numbered requirements at three
  conformance levels (Basic, Standard, Full), a common evidence record, verdict grading
  (release, verify, hold), risk rules derived from FBI and FMCSA guidance, and a mapping to
  CTPAT, TAPA, TIA, and DOT guidance.
keywords:
  - cargo theft
  - freight fraud
  - custody transfer
  - carrier verification
  - cargo seal
  - computer vision
  - supply chain security
  - FMCSA
